WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
Hi. I'm Gus Halwani.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.000
I've followed one thread
for most of my life.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.550
It started with sound.

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.570
I trained as a sound engineer.

5
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.920
Then I got curious about what
the brain does with sound,

6
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.120
so I went to MIT and did my
doctorate in neuroscience,

7
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.520
on how hearing and movement
change with musical training,

8
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.250
and after injury.

9
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.130
After that, I went into learning,
and into building things.

10
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.450
I was Chief Innovation Officer
at The Possible Zone, in Boston.

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.950
I built sensors for race car drivers.

12
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.180
I co-founded a startup
that makes visual stories

13
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.350
for neurodivergent kids
and their families.

14
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.110
So what do I do now? Two things.

15
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.090
One: creative work.

16
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.950
I develop ideas, and I make images,
film, sound, and interactive work.

17
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.690
Two: technology, and change.

18
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.970
I help organizations choose new
technology and actually use it.

19
00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.090
Sometimes that's designing a product.

20
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.130
Sometimes it's leading the build.

21
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.710
Sometimes it's helping a
team change how it works.

22
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.010
I take on select speaking engagements,
workshops, and project work.

23
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.270
If that sounds like you,
reach out through the site.

24
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.390
I'd like to hear what
you're working on.
